obs The fetched path-absence scan found all four sow_fresh paths absent locally and on xy/main, with commits_behind=0. The draft still uses template-manifest.bron; current production uses template-manifest.kyri and has later projection batching and synthetic-input options. Applying the old projector whole would remove newer behavior.
obs Extracted only the parked helper, scan and control into session-output/bakery-freshness-review. The original control ran with TMPDIR inside that directory and passed all 32 legs, failures=0, control_verdict=ok, process exit 0. Transcript: session-output/bakery-freshness-draft-control.txt. This is the draft control result, not a full witness or production projection.
obs A separate synthetic Git pen holds one tracked docs/a file and a hand-built seed/docs/a with identical bytes. The draft helper writes its content receipt; the scan first answers verdict=fresh. Changing only seed/docs/a from mode 0644 to 0755 still answers fresh. Restoring its mode and adding seed/docs/extra-link pointing to a still answers fresh. Lifting the link and adding seed/docs/.sow-content.log containing extra content still answers fresh. Lifting all plants returns fresh. Receipt: session-output/bakery-freshness-review/counterexamples.txt.
obs The helper hashes only find -type f output, so it omits symlinks and mode bits. Its ! -name .sow-content.log predicate excludes that basename at every depth, although only the root receipt should be excluded. These three counterexamples contradict the draft's promise to identify the projected tree exactly. The 32 existing controls test none of them.
obs Disposition: preserve the nine-version family for revision. Before reuse, bind the declared filesystem state, exclude only the actual receipt path, and add controls for each demonstrated false acceptance. Review hash-pipeline failure propagation and the current projector input closure before any implementation; those are static concerns here, not additional executed counterexamples. Public seed publishing stays manual.
